@startuml tool_system_architecture
' Pre-change baseline: CampusClaw merge base d649866a6cae967ace18ceaeb9597edd47e5721e.
' Reviewed tool assembly baseline: CampusClaw 8e4d9914106aab8745e6cba801047af816ce5132.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSessionFactory.java, create
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/builtin/DefaultConfiguredToolAssembler.java, assemble
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/SearchTools.java, execute
' Architecture change: the source-evidence types did not exist at the pre-change baseline.
' Observed at reviewed baseline: one session factory serves Runtime, Cron, and Child entry points.
' Design reason: host lifecycle stays outside the shared session while tool semantics remain identical.
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
title Managed Agent Tool System v2

component "Runtime HTTP Host" as Runtime
component "Cron Host" as Cron
component "Child Execution" as Child
component "AgentSessionFactory" as Factory
component "ManagedAgentSession" as Session
component "ConfiguredToolAssembler" as Assembler
component "BuiltInToolFactory" as ToolFactory
component "AgentRuntimeManager" as RuntimeManager
component "MateToolClient" as Mate
component "MateToolSessionState" as State
component "MateToolExecutor" as Executor

Runtime --> RuntimeManager : prepare(agentId)
Cron --> RuntimeManager : prepare at trigger
Child --> RuntimeManager : prepare child
Runtime --> Factory : RUNTIME
Cron --> Factory : CRON
Child --> Factory : CHILD_AGENT
Factory --> Session : create isolated instance
Factory --> Assembler
Assembler --> ToolFactory : configured fixed-name set
Factory --> State : create per Session
Assembler --> State : create Agent direct proxies
ToolFactory --> State : create SearchTools and CallTool
State *-- Executor : shared trusted resolver and executor
Executor --> Mate : trusted resolve and execute
note right of Session
  Isolated messages, tools,
  workspace, hooks, cancel domain,
  and Mate session cache
end note
@enduml

@startuml mate_credential_flow
' Pre-change implementation baseline: CampusClaw 320d790726a70aada6100052952d5494d2a378ac.
' Credential-completeness pre-change baseline: CampusClaw 6a331d3477df23f8404582c3922b55c265530605.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java, submit
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeRequestContext.java, mateCredentials
' Tool routing baseline: CampusClaw 8e4d9914106aab8745e6cba801047af816ce5132.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/MateToolResolver.java, loadAgentTools, loadSkillTool
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java, invokeTool
' Observed behavior: the pre-change client forwarded three execution credential headers to discovery and execute.
' Architecture change: Claw does not validate credential completeness; Mate validates the real execute request.
' Security hardening: discovery receives no credentials; only execute receives provided non-empty header values.
' Java divergence: pi has no corresponding Mate credential flow.
skinparam shadowing false
title Mate Tool Execution Credential Flow

actor "mate-service" as Caller
participant "RuntimeEventController" as Controller
participant "RuntimeEventService" as Service
participant "RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry" as Registry
participant "AgentSessionFactory" as Factory
participant "MateToolResolver" as Resolver
participant "MateToolExecutor" as Executor
participant "HttpMateToolClient" as Client
participant "Child Session" as Child

Caller -> Controller : POST Events\nzero to four credential headers
Controller -> Service : immutable MateCredentials
Service -> Registry : values held for current execution
Registry -> Factory : ManagedAgentSessionRequest
Factory -> Resolver : create via MateToolSessionState
Factory -> Executor : create with current execution values
Resolver -> Client : Agent or Skill metadata without credentials
Executor -> Client : execute once with provided non-empty values
Factory -> Child : use parent execution values
note over Service,Child
  Values are held only during this Agent execution
  and its Child calls.
  Command has a separate HTTP and service path
  and follows the same snapshot rule.
  Never write to database, Event, Prompt,
  model messages, or logs.
  Runtime releases active references after execution.
end note
note over Executor,Client
  Empty and partial snapshots still call execute once.
  Mate validates credentials and returns the result.
  No defaults, Bearer prefix, borrowing, or retry.
end note
@enduml

@startuml agent_workspace_boundary
' Pre-change baseline: CampusClaw merge base d649866a6cae967ace18ceaeb9597edd47e5721e.
' Reviewed implementation baseline: CampusClaw PR commit bf28e72f94f29acd316eb872a250893ed54e3632.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/workspace/WorkspacePathResolver.java, resolveExisting
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/workspace/WorkspacePathResolver.java, revalidateDiscoveredPath
' Security hardening: WorkspacePathResolver did not exist at the pre-change baseline.
' Observed at reviewed baseline: all managed file tools resolve through the Agent workspace boundary.
' Design reason: a managed Agent may read its complete root but never another Agent root.
skinparam shadowing false
title Agent Workspace Boundary

rectangle "agent/agent-a" as RootA {
  component ".campusclaw" as MetaA
  component "business files" as FilesA
}
rectangle "agent/agent-b" as RootB
component "Read / Find / Grep / Ls" as Tools
component "WorkspacePathResolver" as Resolver

Tools --> Resolver : resolve and revalidate
Resolver --> RootA : allow normalized real path
Resolver -[#red,dashed]-> RootB : reject cross-Agent path
Resolver -[#red,dashed]-> RootA : reject any symlink path
note bottom of Resolver
  lexical boundary
  component symlink rejection
  realpath boundary
  traversal-time revalidation
end note
@enduml

@startuml mate_call_refresh
' Implementation baseline: CampusClaw 8e4d9914106aab8745e6cba801047af816ce5132.
' Source evidence: modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java, execute
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/CallTool.java, prepare
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/MateToolResolver.java, resolveSkill, loadSkillTool
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/MateToolExecutor.java, prepareSkill, validateArguments
' Observed behavior: CallTool resolves trusted direct Skill associations and validates business args before the Host hook.
' Design reason: the same immutable prepared invocation crosses permission or confirmation and business execution.
skinparam shadowing false
title CallTool - Permission, Resolution and Single Execution

actor Model
participant "ToolExecutionPipeline" as Pipeline
participant "CallTool / MateToolExecutor" as Call
participant "MateToolResolver" as Resolver
participant "MateToolClient" as Mate

Model -> Pipeline : CallTool({tool, args?})
Pipeline -> Pipeline : validate outer schema
Pipeline -> Call : prepare trusted call
Call -> Resolver : resolveSkill(name)
Resolver -> Resolver : check trusted Skill association
opt definition not cached
  Resolver -> Mate : listSkillTools(associated skillId)
  Mate --> Resolver : metadata without execution credentials
  Resolver -> Resolver : match trusted name and ID\ncache this tool definition
end
Resolver --> Call : resolved tool or error
Call -> Call : validate business args\nfreeze PreparedToolInvocation
Call --> Pipeline : prepared invocation or isError=true
Pipeline -> Pipeline : Host permission\nand required confirmation
Pipeline -> Call : execute same prepared invocation
Call -> Mate : callTool(toolId, frozen args, credentials) once
Mate --> Call : result
Call --> Pipeline : result or failure
Pipeline --> Model : ToolResultMessage
note over Pipeline,Mate
  Any failure stops later steps and returns isError=true.
  Invalid args never request confirmation or execute.
  SearchTools discovery does not add model tools.
  Actual execution is never replayed.
end note
@enduml
